    "kibana.alert.rule.created_at": "2026-10-05T09:22:51.235Z",
    "kibana.alert.rule.created_by": "elastic",
    "kibana.alert.rule.description": "Detects an HTTP POST sent through the proxy directly to an IP address (no hostname in the URL, so destination.domain is absent) over unencrypted HTTP. Malware command-and-control and data-exfiltration channels frequently POST to hard-coded IPs; legitimate software mostly uses hostnames and TLS. Private/CGNAT ranges and Telegram Messenger (which POSTs to raw IPs by design and dominates the baseline) are excluded. Baseline on 2026-10-05: ~540 events/hour from ~70 hosts after exclusions, mostly vendor telemetry (pollmessage, fdsupdate) plus a few one-host beacons worth investigating.",
    "kibana.alert.rule.enabled": true,
    "kibana.alert.rule.exceptions_list": [],
    "kibana.alert.rule.execution.timestamp": "2026-10-09T12:23:38.504Z",
    "kibana.alert.rule.execution.type": "scheduled",
    "kibana.alert.rule.execution.uuid": "7cdf34ac-9a94-7dfd-a2f8-fde674132470",
    "kibana.alert.rule.false_positives": [],
    "kibana.alert.rule.from": "now-11m",
    "kibana.alert.rule.immutable": false,
    "kibana.alert.rule.indices": [
      "acme-logs-squid*"
    ],
    "kibana.alert.rule.interval": "10m",
    "kibana.alert.rule.license": "",
    "kibana.alert.rule.max_signals": 100,
    "kibana.alert.rule.meta.created_from": "CC_Report_Writer proxy baseline 2026-10-05",
    "kibana.alert.rule.name": "Proxy: Plain-HTTP POST to Raw IP Address (Possible C2 Beacon)",
    "kibana.alert.rule.note": "### Investigation Steps\n1. Review `url.original` path and `destination.ip`. Reputation-check the IP (AbuseIPDB, VirusTotal, GreyNoise) and note `destination.as.organization.name` / country.\n2. How many internal hosts POST to this IP? Many hosts + vendor-looking path (pollmessage, fdsupdate, heartbeat) = device telemetry. One host + odd path (e.g. /index.php, /gate.php, random string) = treat as suspected C2.\n3. Check periodicity: regular intervals with similar `source.bytes` strongly suggests a beacon.\n4. Pivot the host in nginx/DNS logs and request an endpoint check.\n\n### False positives\nIoT/printer telemetry, Chinese phone vendor push services, internal services on public IPs. Add confirmed-benign destination IPs to the exception list; alerts are suppressed per source/destination pair for 24h.",
    "kibana.alert.rule.parameters": {
      "alert_suppression": {
        "duration": {
          "unit": "h",
          "value": 24
        },
        "group_by": [
          "source.ip",
          "destination.ip"
        ],
        "missing_fields_strategy": "suppress"
      },
      "author": [
        "ACME"
      ],
      "description": "Detects an HTTP POST sent through the proxy directly to an IP address (no hostname in the URL, so destination.domain is absent) over unencrypted HTTP. Malware command-and-control and data-exfiltration channels frequently POST to hard-coded IPs; legitimate software mostly uses hostnames and TLS. Private/CGNAT ranges and Telegram Messenger (which POSTs to raw IPs by design and dominates the baseline) are excluded. Baseline on 2026-10-05: ~540 events/hour from ~70 hosts after exclusions, mostly vendor telemetry (pollmessage, fdsupdate) plus a few one-host beacons worth investigating.",
      "exceptions_list": [],
      "false_positives": [],
      "filters": [],
      "from": "now-11m",
      "immutable": false,
      "index": [
        "acme-logs-squid*"
      ],
      "investigation_fields": {
        "field_names": [
          "source.ip",
          "destination.ip",
          "url.original",
          "destination.as.organization.name",
          "destination.geo.country_name",
          "source.bytes"
        ]
      },
      "language": "kuery",
      "license": "",
      "max_signals": 100,
      "meta": {
        "created_from": "CC_Report_Writer proxy baseline 2026-10-05"
      },
      "note": "### Investigation Steps\n1. Review `url.original` path and `destination.ip`. Reputation-check the IP (AbuseIPDB, VirusTotal, GreyNoise) and note `destination.as.organization.name` / country.\n2. How many internal hosts POST to this IP? Many hosts + vendor-looking path (pollmessage, fdsupdate, heartbeat) = device telemetry. One host + odd path (e.g. /index.php, /gate.php, random string) = treat as suspected C2.\n3. Check periodicity: regular intervals with similar `source.bytes` strongly suggests a beacon.\n4. Pivot the host in nginx/DNS logs and request an endpoint check.\n\n### False positives\nIoT/printer telemetry, Chinese phone vendor push services, internal services on public IPs. Add confirmed-benign destination IPs to the exception list; alerts are suppressed per source/destination pair for 24h.",
      "query": "network.protocol:\"http\" and http.request.method:\"POST\" and destination.ip:* and not destination.domain:* and not destination.ip:(10.0.0.0/8 or 172.16.0.0/12 or 192.168.0.0/16 or 100.64.0.0/10) and not destination.as.organization.name.keyword:\"Telegram Messenger Inc\"",
